# P6 enterprise theming architecture

**Goal:** One trunk theming system that scales to **many workspaces**, **many tenants**, and **three app surfaces** (admin · portal · marketing) — with the **smallest** moving parts and the **strongest** override chain.

**Reference implementation:** Denali operator admin (`apps/web` + `packages/workspaces/denali/theme/denali-admin.css`).

---

## 1. Industry synthesis (2025–2026)

Research across DTCG/Style Dictionary, Tailwind v4, shadcn monorepos, and multi-tenant SaaS frontends converges on one pattern:

| Principle | Why it wins |
| --------- | ----------- |
| **Three token layers** | Primitives → Semantics → Component/workspace overrides. Components never read raw hex. |
| **Runtime CSS variables** | Tenant + workspace switch without rebuild; zero JS style parsing. |
| **`@theme inline` for colors** | Tailwind utilities (`bg-primary`) track live `var(--primary)` — required for white-label. |
| **Shared package, one Tailwind entry** | Design-token package exports CSS **without** `@import "tailwindcss"`; each app imports Tailwind once. |
| **Attribute-scoped skins** | `[data-workspace-plugin]` / `[data-app-surface]` — no style leakage between workspaces. |
| **Manifest-driven stylesheet ingress** | Workspace owns skin path; registry generator wires apps — no hard-coded imports in layouts. |

**What we deliberately skip (not minimal):**

- Per-tenant CSS file builds (build-time splitting) — admin uses runtime `TenantThemeProvider`; guest uses workspace skin ingress.
- CSS-in-JS theme engines — breaks static/SSR guest pages.
- Flat Tailwind config tokens — v4 `@theme` in CSS is the trunk standard.

---

## 2. Locked architecture — four layers

```text
Layer 0  Primitives     packages/design-tokens (DTCG JSON → CSS --color-*, --space-*)
Layer 1  Shell bridge   shell-bridge.css — @theme inline + shadcn ↔ platform map
Layer 2  Tenant runtime TenantThemeProvider — admin/operator only; guest surfaces skip L2
Layer 3  Workspace skin packages/workspaces/<id>/theme/*.css — scoped overrides + component tokens
```

**DTCG scaffold (R-08):** `packages/design-tokens/dtcg/platform.tokens.json` — validated by `guard-dtcg-tokens.mjs` and kept in sync with `themes/light.css` via `generate-tokens.mjs` + `guard-dtcg-css-sync.mjs`.

### Cascade (most specific wins)

```text
:root / .theme-dark          ← platform semantics (design-tokens)
  ↓
body[data-workspace-plugin] ← workspace palette (denali forest/mist, urban accent, …)
  ↓
body[data-app-surface]      ← surface chrome (portal register vs marketing catalog)
  ↓
TenantThemeProvider (admin) ← tenant primary override (--color-primary); guest uses L3 skin only
  ↓
Component data-* rules      ← registration form, catalog card, operator sidebar
```

**Rule:** TSX and features read **semantic** tokens only (`var(--primary)`, `bg-card`, `text-muted-foreground`). Workspace differences live in **Layer 3 CSS**, not duplicated React.

---

## 3. Package contracts

### 3.1 `@app-tour/design-tokens`

| Export | Role | Imports Tailwind? |
| ------ | ---- | ----------------- |
| `styles.css` | Full platform tokens (admin entry) | No |
| `guest-shell.css` | `index.css` + `shell-bridge.css` + body reset | No |
| `shell-bridge.css` | `@theme inline` + shadcn semantic bridge | No |

**App `globals.css` (every surface):**

```css
@import "@app-tour/design-tokens/guest-shell.css"; /* or styles.css for admin */
@import "tailwindcss";
/* NO page rules here — move to workspace skin */
```

### 3.2 `@app-tour/theme-react`

| App | Provider | Why |
| --- | -------- | --- |
| Admin | `ThemeProviderChain` | CASL + workspace plugin theme + operator dark toggle |
| Portal / Marketing | `PlatformThemeProvider` only (guest) | Workspace skin (L3) owns brand; no `TenantThemeProvider` primary ingress |

### 3.3 Workspace theme bundles

| Workspace | Admin | Portal | Marketing |
| --------- | ----- | ------ | --------- |
| Denali | `denali-admin.css` | `denali-portal.css` | `denali-marketing.css` |
| Urban | `tokens.css` | (future `urban-portal.css`) | (future) |
| Starter | `tokens.css` | — | — |

Manifest keys (`workspace.manifest.json`):

```json
{
  "themeStylesheets": ["theme/denali-admin.css"],
  "guestThemeStylesheets": {
    "portal": ["theme/denali-portal.css"],
    "marketing": ["theme/denali-marketing.css"]
  }
}
```

Generator output:

- `apps/web/src/bootstrap/workspace-theme-stylesheets.generated.ts`
- `apps/portal/src/bootstrap/workspace-guest-theme-stylesheets.generated.ts`
- `apps/marketing/src/bootstrap/workspace-guest-theme-stylesheets.generated.ts`

---

## 4. Body attributes (scope contract)

| Attribute | Set by | Purpose |
| --------- | ------ | ------- |
| `data-workspace-plugin="{pluginId}"` | Layout from host bootstrap | Workspace skin selector |
| `data-app-surface="portal\|marketing"` | Guest layout | Surface-specific component tokens |
| `data-tenant-id` | Admin layout | Ops/debug; guest uses bootstrap in BFF |

**Denali portal skin selector:**

```css
body[data-app-surface="portal"][data-workspace-plugin="denali"] { … }
```

Same pattern for marketing. Urban/starter skins add their own `data-workspace-plugin` block — no cross-workspace imports in apps.

---

## 5. Fields differ per workspace — separate concern

Theming (Layer 0–3) is **visual**. **Field shapes** are workspace-owned in `packages/workspaces/<id>/`:

| Concern | Owner | Example |
| ------- | ----- | ------- |
| Colors, radius, motion | `theme/*.css` | Denali mist page background |
| Form fields, validation | `ui/fields/*`, HTTP routes | Denali `partySize` vs Urban `notes` |
| Registration intake | `apps/portal` shell + SDK dispatch | `buildCatalogRegistrationUpstreamRequest(pluginId)` |

**Do not** solve field differences with CSS alone. **Do not** solve colors in workspace TypeScript.

---

## 6. Minimal vs powerful — decision matrix

| Need | Minimal path | Powerful path (when required) |
| ---- | ------------ | ----------------------------- |
| New workspace color story | Add `theme/<workspace>-<surface>.css` + manifest | + `tokens.css` contract `--ws-color-accent` |
| New guest page layout | `data-*` rules in workspace skin | Promote to `@app-tour/ui-primitives` if ≥3 consumers |
| Tenant rebrand (guest) | Workspace skin CSS | Manifest + theme codegen — not runtime `TenantThemeProvider` |
| Tenant rebrand (admin) | `TenantThemeProvider` / branding settings | Operator preview paths only |
| Dark mode guest | Defer P6 | Mirror admin dual cascade (`html.dark` + `.theme-dark`) |
| New app surface | Copy 2-file pattern: `globals.css` + generated skin ingress | Register `guestThemeStylesheets.<surface>` in manifest |

---

## 7. P6 implementation checklist

```text
✅ design-tokens: shell-bridge.css exported; guest-shell composes it
✅ apps/*/globals.css: imports only (no page-specific rules)
✅ workspace manifest: themeStylesheets + guestThemeStylesheets
✅ generate:workspace-registry → portal + marketing guest stylesheet bundles
✅ layout: data-workspace-plugin + data-app-surface on <body>
✅ denali-portal.css + denali-marketing.css scoped skins (MASTER tokens · Calistoga headings)
✅ portal next.config allowedDevOrigins: *.portal.localhost (Playwright cross-host dev)
✅ Guest portal/marketing: `PlatformThemeProvider` only — see [css-ownership-model.mdoc](../standards/css-ownership-model.mdoc)
✅ specs: guest-theme-stack + workspace skin contract · UI specs in docs/workspaces/denali/
```

---

## 8. Verification

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
pnpm --filter @app-tour/design-tokens run build
pnpm --filter @apps/portal run test
pnpm --filter @apps/marketing run test
```

Admin reference (unchanged):

```bash
pnpm --filter @apps/web test -- test/denali-admin-theme.spec.ts
```

